{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzE5MjU1","is_bot":false,"login":"adamissac","name":"Adam Issac"},"body":"## Task\n\nTask ID(s): ops follow-up (prod outage 2026-10-28)\nPillar / subsystem: infra\n\n## What changed and why\n\nAt 2026-10-28 20:13 UTC Railway removed both the `ari-ai` and `Postgres` deployments. The API then served Railway's \"Application not found\" 404 until 2026-10-30, when they were redeployed. Login, GitHub connect and assessments were all down. The hourly `storage-watch` still reported success, because it only checks volumes and backups.\n\n- `scripts/ops/uptime_watch.py` checks `GET /healthz` (must be 200 with `status: ok`) and that every Railway service in the token's environment has a latest deployment in `SUCCESS`/`SLEEPING`. If either check fails it opens or updates `[ops-alert] Production is down`, deduplicated by marker, and closes the issue on recovery. It reuses `storage_watch`'s Railway GraphQL client (including the Cloudflare curl fallback) and `GitHubClient`.\n- `.github/workflows/uptime-watch.yml` runs every 15 min with the existing `RAILWAY_TOKEN` Actions secret, and runs the unit tests on PRs.\n\nThe watchdog only alerts; it never redeploys or makes any other change to prod.\n\n## Evidence it works\n\n```\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/ops\nOK   (storage + uptime suites)\n$ RAILWAY_TOKEN=<project token> python3 scripts/ops/uptime_watch.py   # against live prod after restore\n| ari-ai | SUCCESS |\n| Postgres | SUCCESS |\n## Problems\n- None          exit=0\n$ uv run ruff check scripts/ops tests/ops && uv run ruff format --check scripts/ops tests/ops\nAll checks passed! / 4 files already formatted\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Scope matches the task; no unrelated changes\n- [x] Tests added/updated and passing locally (list above)\n- [x] Uses `shared/` contracts; no locally redefined shared models (n/a)\n- [x] Contract change? no\n- [x] Executes code / sends network traffic / changes state? read-only Railway + health GETs; issue writes only\n- [x] No secrets, customer code, or third-party exploit details\n- [x] Docs updated: `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [x] UI/docs claims do not exceed what the code actually does\n- [x] No attribution trailers in commits\n\n## Risks / follow-ups\n\n- The workflow alerts but does not self-heal.\n- The cause of the removal is unknown. Railway's event log records `removed Deployment` for both services with no actor, so billing, usage limits and a manual removal are all still possible.\n\nLink to Devin session: https://app.devin.ai/sessions/7d173df1be5442b8a11cbc8b6e5630a0\nOpen in Devin Desktop: https://app.devin.ai/desktop/session/7d173df1be5442b8a11cbc8b6e5630a0?variant=devin\nRequested by: @adamissac","files":[{"path":".github/workflows/uptime-watch.yml","additions":47,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/ops/uptime_watch.py","additions":175,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"tests/ops/test_uptime_watch.py","additions":115,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"}],"headRefName":"fix/adam/uptime-watchdog","headRefOid":"56204e4aa073540125489ac7e54a080ec6abea3d","mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"BEHIND","number":723,"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-30T00:17:46Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/adamissac/ari-ai/actions/runs/40978782385/job/123813299432","name":"pin","startedAt":"2026-10-30T00:17:46Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Ari candidate review"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-30T00:18:07Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/adamissac/ari-ai/actions/runs/40978782246/job/123813295289","name":"backend-tests","startedAt":"2026-10-30T00:17:48Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"backend"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-30T00:18:09Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/adamissac/ari-ai/actions/runs/40978782126/jo